  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Public Internal Audit Function</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strategic Objectives  The grant will contribute to the efforts of the Turkish Government on improving the internal audit function for better governance and accountability in the public sector. The grant will support the implementation of the internal audit framework as stipulated in the Public Financial Management and Control Law. The project will be a continuation of a series of tasks and activities undertaken under the Programmatic Public Expenditure Review which formed the umbrella for many public financial management activities in the past several years. Description The proposed activities aim to support the Internal Audit Coordination Board (IACB) in the implementation of its 2011-2013 Public Internal Audit Startegy Paper. The support provided by the grant would be twofold: enhance the capacity of the IACB in its role as a regulatory and coordinating/monitoring body and strengthen the technical capabilities of internal auditors. The project activities will be geared toward enhancing the technical capacity of the internal auditors and supporting the implementation of the internal audit regulations. Major activities will include specialized assignments on performance measurement and information systems audits in pilot fields, knowledge-sharing seminars and dissemination workshops, quality assurance reviews and preparation of guidance notes/manuals. TF011904</narrative>
  </description>
